ss successfully expanded the database scope beyond the user's initial subset.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Clarification on dataset expansion","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:37:16.106Z","title":"User inquiry regarding new competition data","type":"conversation"},"obs_mpv71f6v_3d37db125d1e":{"concepts":["SQL","PostgreSQL","Data validation","Database schema inspection"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Database: scoru at postgresql://localhost:5432","Query aggregates matches per competition using LEFT JOIN on sports_matches","Data reveals significant variance in match counts (e.g., Ligue 1: 620, Serie A: 762, Premier League: 0/760)"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpv71f6v_3d37db125d1e","importance":4,"narrative":"Executed a SQL query to inspect the distribution of matches across various sports competitions. The output confirms the relationship between sports_competitions and sports_matches, highlighting potential data quality issues or migration artifacts in the Premier League records.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Inspection of the scoru database schema and data distribution","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:37:23.588Z","title":"Query sports competitions and match counts","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpv7gz7p_cbfbedf678fa":{"concepts":["user input","prompt engineering"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User input consisted only of the character \"A\"","No actionable request or command was provided"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpv7gz7p_cbfbedf678fa","importance":1,"narrative":"The user initiated a prompt submission with only a single character. As the input is incomplete and lacks context, no specific tasks can be performed.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Empty or truncated prompt received","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:49:29.388Z","title":"User Input Incomplete","type":"conversation"},"obs_mpv7htx0_f69da79dd927":{"concepts":["API documentation","data-pipeline","allowlisting","request validation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added 'all' boolean field to API request body for bypass of Ccd allowlist","Updated doc comments to reflect use of DEFAULT_ALLOW_CCDS in cron workflows","Explicitly documented that 'all: true' enables greedy mode for data ingestion"],"files":["src/pages/api/data-pipeline/pull-by-date.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7htx0_f69da79dd927","importance":4,"narrative":"Updated the JSDoc comments in the data-pipeline API route to accurately reflect the recently added 'all' parameter. This ensures external consumers understand how to override the default restrictive allowlist for one-off data pulls.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Added support for 'all' flag and documented default allowlist behavior","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:50:09.177Z","title":"Update API documentation for pull-by-date endpoint","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpv7i20y_3d4f8e1bb753":{"concepts":["API filtering","Data ingestion pipeline","Allowlisting"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Introduced DEFAULT_ALLOW_CCDS as a Set of string country/confederation codes.","Includes leagues (Top 5 + Romania), European club competitions, and major international tournaments (including World Cup 2026).","The allowlist prevents excessive data ingestion from non-relevant Livescore stages."],"files":["src/pages/api/data-pipeline/pull-by-date.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7i20y_3d4f8e1bb753","importance":5,"narrative":"Added a formal allowlist constant to the data pipeline API route to restrict imported competitions to a predefined set. This ensures the ingestion process remains performant and focused on relevant data, while maintaining support for manual overrides via the API request body.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Adding allowlist constant for Livescore competition filtering","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:50:19.687Z","title":"Define DEFAULT_ALLOW_CCDS in data pipeline","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpv7i7y3_102835a6a8ac":{"concepts":["API filtering","allowlist pattern","greedy mode","data-pipeline"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Added boolean bypassAllowlist derived from body.all","Updated allow logic to ignore DEFAULT_ALLOW_CCDS when bypassAllowlist is true","Converted allow list to a Set for efficient filtering"],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/pages/api/data-pipeline/pull-by-date.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7i7y3_102835a6a8ac","importance":5,"narrative":"Modified the API route to support a greedy mode where the default allowlist is bypassed. This enables the data-pipeline to pull match data for all competitions when requested, rather than being restricted to the predefined core set of leagues.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Adding greedy mode support to pull-by-date API","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:50:27.358Z","title":"Implement 'all' bypass for data-pipeline allowlist","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpv7ic1f_dc00b4369c99":{"concepts":["Set lookup optimization","API data filtering","performance refactoring"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Changed `allow.includes(ccd)` to `allow.has(ccd)` in the data pipeline loop.","The `allow` variable is defined as a `Set` in the surrounding scope, making `has` the correct and more performant lookup method."],"files":["/Users/torel/code/2025/scoru/src/pages/api/data-pipeline/pull-by-date.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7ic1f_dc00b4369c99","importance":4,"narrative":"Fixed a performance bug where the `allow` variable was being treated as an array despite being initialized as a `Set`. By switching to `.has()`, the filtering logic now correctly utilizes the O(1) lookup complexity of a Set.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Refactored array inclusion to set lookup","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:50:32.663Z","title":"Optimize allowlist lookup in data pipeline","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpv7jezk_9707ca322c50":{"concepts":["database maintenance","data integrity","transactional safety","script automation"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Implemented an allow-list based competition cleanup script.","Script handles dry-run by default; requires --apply flag for execution.","Logic encapsulates deletions within a single transaction to ensure data integrity.","Script preserves teams while removing orphaned competitions and their associated match data."],"files":["scripts/maintenance/prune-competitions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7jezk_9707ca322c50","importance":6,"narrative":"Created a maintenance script to clear unwanted competition data from the database, which was previously polluted by greedy ingestion. The script classifies existing entries against an explicit allow-list, providing a summary of candidates for deletion before execution.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"scripts/maintenance/prune-competitions.ts","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:51:23.140Z","title":"Created maintenance script to prune database noise","type":"file_write"},"obs_mpv7jiq0_b4cd2ea06ae4":{"concepts":["database maintenance","foreign key cascade","data lifecycle management","dry-run verification"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Identified 1684 matches scheduled for deletion","Script cascades deletes through event, lineup, and statistics tables via foreign keys","Actionable via --apply flag","Execution involves cleanup of 88 competition mappings and 1684 match mappings"],"files":["scripts/maintenance/prune-competitions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7jiq0_b4cd2ea06ae4","importance":5,"narrative":"Executed a dry-run of the database maintenance script to purge obsolete competition data. The output confirms that foreign key constraints are correctly configured for cascading deletions and provides an accurate count of affected records before committing the destructive operation.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Verified scope of database maintenance script","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:51:27.983Z","title":"Dry-run competition pruning","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpv7jm8y_03265af8c71c":{"concepts":["database maintenance","data pruning","PostgreSQL","TSX"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Script identified 123 total competitions in database","Pruning logic targets 88 competitions for removal, keeping 35","Dry-run confirmed high match count impact in Ecuador (765) and Algeria (620)"],"files":["scripts/maintenance/prune-competitions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7jm8y_03265af8c71c","importance":5,"narrative":"The script was executed in a dry-run mode to assess the impact of pruning stale competition data from the PostgreSQL database. The output confirms that a significant portion of competitions (88 out of 123) are slated for removal, which will help reduce the overall database size and match record count.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Execution of maintenance script for cleaning competition data","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:51:32.552Z","title":"Database Maintenance: Prune Competitions Dry-Run","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpv7jx6y_fd4fba554d2e":{"concepts":["database maintenance","data pruning","SQL cascading deletes","PostgreSQL transaction"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Deleted 1,684 matches and associated cascade records (events, lineups, stats).","Removed 'Women's World Cup Qualification' competition data.","Execution performed within a single database transaction.","Removed 88 competition mappings and 1,684 match mappings."],"files":["scripts/maintenance/prune-competitions.ts"],"id":"obs_mpv7jx6y_fd4fba554d2e","importance":6,"narrative":"The maintenance script successfully pruned obsolete competition data and its associated cascade records from the Scoru database. This operation significantly reduced the dataset size by removing 1,684 matches and related mappings, ensuring data integrity via transactional execution.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Performed cleanup of 1,684 matches and related records","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:51:46.734Z","title":"Executed database maintenance script: prune-competitions.ts","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpv7k1yi_908a75aff8eb":{"concepts":["SQL aggregation","database verification","data pruning","PostgreSQL"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Database: scoru","England has 2 competitions and 760 matches.","Europe has 9 competitions and 1788 matches.","Germany, International, Romania, and Spain statistics verified."],"files":["N/A"],"id":"obs_mpv7k1yi_908a75aff8eb","importance":5,"narrative":"Executed a SQL query to verify the data integrity of sports competitions and matches following a pruning operation. The output confirms the distribution of competitions and match counts across various geographical regions.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Aggregated competition and match counts by country","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:51:52.907Z","title":"Verify post-prune database state","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpv7k66f_a303d55b32ab":{"concepts":["SQL","PostgreSQL","data auditing","schema analysis"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Queried postgresql://localhost:5432/scoru","Joined sports_competitions with match counts from sports_matches","Identified 35 total competition entries","Noted duplicates in Premier League entries and detailed match distribution across international/league formats"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpv7k66f_a303d55b32ab","importance":4,"narrative":"Performed a SQL query to audit the sports competitions database schema. The results reveal the distribution of match counts across various international and domestic leagues, highlighting data anomalies such as duplicate Premier League entries.","sessionId":"348be068-f172-4e96-a1c6-f633358ff2cc","subtitle":"Database inspection of scoru schema","timestamp":"2026-06-01T12:51:58.378Z","title":"Query sports_competitions and match counts","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpv7kjjw_58db6f6789a2":{"concepts":["PostgreSQL query","data verification","schema auditing"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Database: scoru, Table: sports_competitions","Query returned 2 results, both 'Premier League' from 'England'","Target leagues 'Serie A' and 'Ligue 1' were not found in the result set